{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type FieldWithValue<TFieldValue> = FieldApi<any, TFieldValue, any, any, any>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/types.public.ts#L52","children":[{"type":"text","value":"types.public.ts:52"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A field API that preserves its value type while erasing its name, error, and\nowning form types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use it for reusable value-specific UI or helpers that should accept the same\nvalue type at any field path. Value reads and updates remain typed without\ntying the reusable code to one path or form shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfieldvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFieldValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFieldValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The value type preserved across field reads and update methods."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function trimField(field: FieldWithValue<string>) {\n  field.handleChange((value) => value.trim())\n}","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfieldvalue","text":"TFieldValue","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype FieldWithValue<TFieldValue> = FieldApi<any, TFieldValue, any, any, any>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [types.public.ts:52](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/types.public.ts#L52)\n\nA field API that preserves its value type while erasing its name, error, and\nowning form types.\n\nUse it for reusable value-specific UI or helpers that should accept the same\nvalue type at any field path. Value reads and updates remain typed without\ntying the reusable code to one path or form shape.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFieldValue\n\n`TFieldValue`\n\nThe value type preserved across field reads and update methods.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nfunction trimField(field: FieldWithValue<string>) {\n  field.handleChange((value) => value.trim())\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: FieldWithValue\ntitle: FieldWithValue\n---\n\n```ts\ntype FieldWithValue<TFieldValue> = FieldApi<any, TFieldValue, any, any, any>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [types.public.ts:52](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/types.public.ts#L52)\n\nA field API that preserves its value type while erasing its name, error, and\nowning form types.\n\nUse it for reusable value-specific UI or helpers that should accept the same\nvalue type at any field path. Value reads and updates remain typed without\ntying the reusable code to one path or form shape.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFieldValue\n\n`TFieldValue`\n\nThe value type preserved across field reads and update methods.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nfunction trimField(field: FieldWithValue<string>) {\n  field.handleChange((value) => value.trim())\n}\n```\n"}
